  "summary_en": "Binding Malaysian Civil Aviation Directive setting standards and certification procedures for agricultural drone operations, including Aerial Work Certificates, operator management systems, airworthiness, registration, remote pilot competency and pesticide dispensing rules. Operations are limited to VLOS/EVLOS, and autonomous operations are currently prohibited.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "No agricultural UAS activity without a CAAM-issued Aerial Work Certificate (private or commercial).",
   "Autonomous operations (no remote pilot ability to intervene) are not allowed; VLOS/EVLOS only, below 400 ft AGL, 50 m from uninvolved persons.",
   "Operators must maintain third-party liability insurance and a safety management system with nominated post holders.",
   "Pesticides must be DOA/LRMP-approved; remote pilots need RCoC with dispensing module.",
   "Phased certification: pre-application, formal application, document evaluation, demonstration/inspection, certification; audits and enforcement."
  ],
